A||N||13||BlackARROW||Headlight Flap in the Wind||||11||
Z||000000||BlackARROW||04-30-2001||08:42 PM||||Anyone found a good solution for Headlight flap that opens in the wind?  I spoke to a friend who has an SE, and he has the same problem as me.  I thought you'd have experience the same **** . <P>I've had that problem once at 85 mph, but I got it two times at 100 mph, with a side wind.  That time I had to slowdown below the 80 to get it back in place.  It's like it cups the wind, and lifts.  But just the cover, just the flap.   It really supprises when it happens.  I just down want to lose it.  At 100 mph, it's just starting to get windy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>BlackARROW<BR>Fiero 2M4 '85||||reg||11
Z||000001||Oreif||04-30-2001||08:53 PM||||Solution:<BR>Vent the hood. <P>Do a search for hood vents and see the many styles. This will release pressure under the hood above the radiator that causes the popping headlight covers.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||PBJ||04-30-2001||10:12 PM||||I have seen a system on the net and I spent some time looking but can not find it.  I looked like a cable and pully system-this site offered alot of other ideas too.  I do believe if you go to <A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fieroproject.com</A>  and then go to links and then fiero secrets it is some where there.  I have never had this problem, so I never paid much attention.||||reg||1
Z||000003||rogergarrison||04-30-2001||10:27 PM||||flush headlites, nothing blows up on mine even at 150 mph<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=9116379&p=34556781"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||DaveL||05-01-2001||08:02 AM||||Check the undersides of the two doors and compare them. There should be two metal rods that maintain tension downward on these doors. If one or both are missing, they can fly up at inopertune moments.||||reg||1
Z||000005||1FST2M6||05-01-2001||08:19 AM||||did somone say hoodvent?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstintake1.JPG">   <P>or if you don't wanna do that <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A>  and get their headlight restraints. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Slammed Fiero||05-01-2001||08:35 AM||||Chris west sells a nice set up for flapping headlight doors. It looks to be a nice clean mod...<P>DOH ..I read lots...<P>Anyway Chris's mod is a vinyl (I think) coated braided wire that attaches to the bottom cover of the headlight assembly (looks like a tray) then to the top of the door.<P>JM <p>[This message has been edited by Slammed Fiero (edited 05-01-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||Old Lar||05-01-2001||09:33 AM||||Don't drive at over 100 mph!  No headlight cover lift at slower speeds.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Galen||05-01-2001||12:39 PM||||Se ya'll.. he likes his hole ..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Galen - 1988 Hawaiian Orchid Coupe - <A HREF="http://myfiero.spinrpg.com/" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero Website</A><BR><A HREF="http://www.spinrpg.com/" TARGET=_blank>Spinrpg.com - Free URL & e-mail Forwarding</A>||||reg||1
